`md list` prints an ABSOLUTE path in every record, and the harness runs each
case in a scratch directory whose name is random, so a line holding a path can
never be pinned byte for byte. Cases that list at least one file therefore pipe
the output through `md lines`, which selects the lines that hold no path.

--key prints one `path<TAB>value` line per file that HOLDS the key. Of the three
files here only alpha.md has a `title`, so one line is printed and `md lines
--count` reports 2: the one line plus the final newline.

The value half of that line cannot be pinned on its own, because the path in
front of it is absolute and lives in a randomly named scratch directory.
